'''Kenepuru''' will be a future parliamentary [[New Zealand electorates|electorate]] used for the first time in the [[2026 New Zealand general election]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Report of the Representation Commission 2025 |url=https://elections.nz/assets/pagecomponent-file-files/REPORT-OF-THE-REPRESENTATION-COMMISSION-2025-WEB.pdf |access-date=8 August 2025 |website=Electoral Commission |publisher=Electoral Commission}}</ref> It is focused on northern [[Wellington]] and southern [[Porirua]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=9 August 2025 |title=Call for Rongotai electorate to get its name back |url=https://wellington.scoop.co.nz/?p=173018 |access-date=15 August 2025 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Electorate boundaries finalised |url=https://elections.nz/media-and-news/2025/electorate-boundaries-finalised/ |access-date=15 August 2025 |website=Elections |language=en-NZ}}</ref>

==Population centres==
The Kenepuru electorate is centered on the [[Kenepuru]] suburb of [[Porirua]]. It reaches north through [[Porirua Central|Porirua city centre]] to [[Onepoto, Wellington|Onepoto]] and [[Tītahi Bay|Titahi Bay]] in the west and [[Papakōwhai]] and [[Ascot Park, New Zealand|Ascot Park]] in the east. Facing south, the electorate encompasses the major [[Wellington]] suburbs of [[Tawa, New Zealand|Tawa]] and [[Johnsonville, New Zealand|Johnsonville]], as well as the rural community of [[Ohariu, New Zealand|Ohariu]].<ref>{{cite book |title=Report of the Representation Commission 2025 |url=https://elections.nz/assets/pagecomponent-file-files/REPORT-OF-THE-REPRESENTATION-COMMISSION-2025-WEB.pdf |isbn=978-0-473-75233-0 |publisher=Representation Commission |access-date=3 September 2025 |page=18 |date=8 August 2025 }}</ref>

== History ==
The 2025 boundary review required a reduction in North Island electorates by one to reflect nationwide population shifts. The three Wellington City electorates ([[Rongotai (electorate)|Rongotai]], [[Wellington Central (electorate)|Wellington Central]] and [[Ōhāriu (electorate)|Ōhāriu]]) were all underpopulated. All were abolished with flow-on effects for the wider region. The [[Mana (electorate)|Mana electorate]] centred on Porirua was also abolished, with its population divided between Kenepuru and [[Kapiti (electorate)|Kapiti]].<ref>{{cite book |url=https://elections.nz/assets/pagecomponent-file-files/REPORT-OF-THE-REPRESENTATION-COMMISSION-2025-WEB.pdf |title=Report of the Representation Commission 2025 |date=8 August 2025 |publisher=Representation Commission |isbn=978-0-473-75233-0 |page=18 |access-date=21 September 2025}}</ref>

==Election results==
===2026 election===
The [[2026 New Zealand general election|next election]] will be held on 7 November 2026. Candidates for Kenepuru are listed at ''[[Candidates in the 2026 New Zealand general election by electorate#Kenepuru|Candidates in the 2026 New Zealand general election by electorate § Kenepuru]]''. Official results will be available after 27 November 2026.<ref name="ge2026_dates">{{Cite web |last= |date=2026 |title=Key dates |url=https://vote.nz/2026-general-election/about/overview/key-dates |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260415030403/https://vote.nz/2026-general-election/about/overview/key-dates |archive-date=15 April 2026 |access-date=27 April 2026 |website=Vote NZ}}</ref>
